# Netlify redirect rules for SmartFintool
#
# ORDER MATTERS. The classic SPA rule (/* /index.html 200) must NOT be used
# here: it would shadow every prerendered route, so /swp would serve the
# homepage HTML and undo the whole point of prerendering. Netlify already
# serves dist/swp/index.html for /swp automatically, so we only need:
#   1. host canonicalisation (www -> apex),
#   2. legacy URL cleanup,
#   3. a 404 fallback for genuinely unknown paths.

# ── 1. Canonical host: force apex + https ───────────────────────────────────
http://smartfintool.com/*    https://smartfintool.com/:splat    301!
http://www.smartfintool.com/*  https://smartfintool.com/:splat  301!
https://www.smartfintool.com/* https://smartfintool.com/:splat  301!

# ── 2. Legacy / mistaken URLs that were live in schema and internal links ──
/simple-interest-calculator   /simple      301
/compound-interest-calculator /compound    301
/sip-calculator               /            301
/swp-calculator               /swp         301
/lumpsum-calculator           /lumpsum     301
/calculators                  /            301
/blog                         /resources   301
/index.html                   /            301

# ── 3. Unknown paths get a real 404, not a soft-200 ────────────────────────
/*  /404.html  404
